HEADER CONVENTION
=================

Every new source file authored for this project SHOULD begin with an SPDX
identifier as the first comment, before the package clause.

Go:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
    // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Win's VPN Inc.

    package carrier

Where a Go build constraint is present it must remain the first line, followed
by a blank line, then the SPDX block:

    //go:build linux

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
    // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Win's VPN Inc.

    package directawg

Shell, Python, YAML and other hash-comment files:

    # SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
    # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Win's VPN Inc.

C, C++, Objective-C, Swift, Java, Kotlin:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
    // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Win's VPN Inc.

Rules:

  1. Use the SPDX form. Do not paste the full licence text into source files.

  2. Use "AGPL-3.0-or-later". Do not use the deprecated "AGPL-3.0" identifier
     alone.

  3. Do not put a year range on individual files and do not update years on
     edit. A single copyright year of first publication is sufficient and
     churning years across thousands of files produces noise without legal
     benefit.

  4. Do not name individual authors in file headers. Copyright is held by
     Win's VPN Inc. under the CLA. Attribution of individuals belongs in the
     commit history, not in file headers.

  5. Generated files should carry the same header plus a line identifying the
     generator, so a reviewer can tell not to edit them by hand.


THIRD-PARTY FILES ARE THE EXCEPTION
===================================

Files derived from third-party code MUST NOT carry the Win's VPN Inc. AGPL
header alone. They MUST preserve the upstream licence and copyright.

Files in internal/masque/ that are derived from github.com/quic-go/masque-go
carry:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
    // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2024 Marten Seemann
    //
    // Derived from github.com/quic-go/masque-go v0.4.0.
    // See UPSTREAM.md in this directory for provenance and local changes.

Winn-authored files in that same directory, which have no upstream counterpart,
carry the ordinary AGPL header. internal/masque/LICENSE and
internal/masque/UPSTREAM.md must not be removed or modified.

When adding any third-party or third-party-derived file:

  - preserve its original licence text in the directory that contains it;
  - record provenance (upstream project, version, commit) in an UPSTREAM.md
    alongside it, following the pattern in internal/masque/;
  - add an entry to NOTICE;
  - confirm the licence is compatible with both AGPL-3.0 outbound distribution
    and commercial relicensing before merging.

A licence that permits AGPL redistribution but not commercial relicensing is
not acceptable in this tree, because it would silently break the dual-licensing
model.


